PyDoc_STRVAR(__pyx_doc_10selectolax_6lexbor_10LexborNode_48insert_child, "LexborNode.insert_child(signatures, args, kwargs, defaults, _fused_sigindex={})\n\nInsert a node inside (at the end of) the current Node.\n\nParameters\n----------\nvalue : str, bytes or Node\n    The text or Node instance to insert inside the Node.\n    When a text string is passed, it\047s treated as text. All HTML tags will be escaped.\n    Convert and pass the ``Node`` object when you want to work with HTML.\nmove : bool, optional\n    When ``True``, the ``Node`` object is moved instead of copied: it is\n    removed from its current position and placed here. Defaults to ``False``.\n\nExamples\n--------\n\n>>> tree = LexborHTMLParser(\047<div>Get <img src=\"\"></div>\047)\n>>> div = tree.css_first(\047div\047)\n>>> div.insert_child(\047Laptop\047)\n>>> tree.body.child.html\n\047<div>Get <img src=\"\">Laptop</div>\047\n\n>>> html_parser = LexborHTMLParser(\047<div>Get <span alt=\"Laptop\"> <div>Laptop</div> </span></div>\047)\n>>> html_parser2 = LexborHTMLParser(\047<div>Test</div>\047)\n>>> span_node = html_parser.css_first(\047span\047)\n>>> span_node.insert_child(html_parser2.body.child)\n<div>Get <span alt=\"Laptop\"> <div>Laptop</div> <div>Test</div> </span></div>\047");
